    "q-349464": {
      "dom_id": "step-q349464",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given that $r(t)=⟨3{t}^{4}-7t+1,\\,8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,$ what is ${r}^{′}(t)?$\n\n${r}^{′}(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$",
      "worked_solution": "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=3{t}^{4}-7t+1,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=12{t}^{3}-7.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12{t}^{3}-7,\\,8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
