    "q-50377": {
      "dom_id": "step-q50377",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Given that $r(t)=⟨4t-10,\\,3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(t)=$",
      "worked_solution": "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=4t-10,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=4.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{3}{t}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,\\frac{3}{t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
