    "q-347967": {
      "dom_id": "step-q347967",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Determine ${f}^{″}(t)$ given that $f(t)={e}^{5-2t}\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\,j-3{t}^{4}\\,k.$\n\n${f}^{″}(t)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$j\\,\\,-$\n{{field-3}}\n$k$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{5-2t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t))\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-3{t}^{4})\\,k \\\\  & =-2{e}^{5-2t}\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\,j-12{t}^{3}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThen, we calculate ${f}^{″}(t)$ by differentiating ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2{e}^{5-2t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t))\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-12{t}^{3})\\,k \\\\  & =-2(-2{e}^{5-2t})\\,i+3(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t))\\,j-12(3{t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =4{e}^{5-2t}\\,i-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\,j-36{t}^{2}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
