    "q-75033": {
      "dom_id": "step-q75033",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Given that $r(t)=⟨4{t}^{3}-t,\\,7t-3{t}^{4}⟩,$ ${r}^{″}(t)=$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t)=4{t}^{3}-t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =12{t}^{2}-1 \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =24t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=7t-3{t}^{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =7-12{t}^{3} \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =-36{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨24t,\\,-36{t}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-75033-a",
